    "https://www.usw.edu/careers": {
      "title": "uSW Careers",
      "description": "CAREERS | USW top of page Apply Now! Admissions Questions? ABOUT NEWS ADMISSIONS ACADEMICS Athletics STUDENT LIFE CAREERS More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Community More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. uSW Careers Welcome to the University of the Southwest’s Careers page!  We have a great team of employees and are always looking forward to adding new personnel who will become great assets to our team. The Vice President of Human Resources is the designated individual who can assist all interested applicants with questions regarding employment, benefits, policies, and employment opportunities. Vice President of Human Resources Veronica torrez vtorrez@usw.edu (575) 492 - 2146 Office hours: 7:00 AM - 4:00 PM, Monday - Thursday; 8:00 AM - 12:00 PM, Friday Office location: Human Resources, Mabee Teaching & Learning Center (MTL) Faculty Openings Click Here! Staff Openings Click Here! Employee Benefits Click Here! University of the Southwest participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires USW to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. University of the Southwest is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant on the basis of race, age, disability, religion, color, sex or national origin, or any other basis prohibited by local, state, or federal law. ​ Applicants with a primary residence in one of the following states are NOT eligible for employment at USW: Ohio, Oregon, North Dakota, Washington, Wyoming Join us in our mission? DONATE Connect with us on social media! Questions, Comments, Concerns, or Complaints? Click Here CONTACT US IN PERSON: 6610 N Lovington Highway Hobbs, NM 88240 M-Th: 8AM-5PM, F: 8AM-12PM (MST) by phone: Toll Free: (800) 530 - 4400 Locally: (575) 392 - 6561 Campus Directory BY MAIL: University of the Southwest 6610 N Lovington Hwy Hobbs, NM 88240 Consumer Information FILE DIRECTORY Non-discrimination policy University of the Southwest admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the institution. USW does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, physical handicap, or sex in the administration of its educational policies, admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletics and other university-administered programs. Notice any issues with our website? Let us know! © 2023 by University of the Southwest bottom of page"
